      "slug": "club",
      "page_level_design_instruction": "The Club page serves as the definitive authoritative overview of Courtside & Crown \u2014 a richly layered, heritage-driven editorial experience that earns the trust of prospective members through storytelling, credibility, and clarity. The page must feel like a distinguished club brochure brought to life digitally, blending gravitas with warmth.\n\n**Overall Page Rhythm & Section Flow:**\nThe page opens with a grand, symmetrical page header that anchors the heritage identity. It then descends into a vertical timeline section that narrates the club's century of history. The coaching team is presented in a card grid at mid-page, followed by a clearly differentiated pricing/membership tier grid. The page closes with a facilities feature grid before handing off to the global footer. This rhythm moves from emotional storytelling \u2192 historical proof \u2192 human credibility \u2192 commercial conversion \u2192 physical reassurance \u2014 a deliberate funnel that respects the audience's decision-making journey.\n\n**Color Usage Across the Page:**\n- Primary background: Crown Ivory (#F5F0E8) for the majority of the page body, lending the parchment warmth appropriate to a heritage institution.\n- The page header section uses a deep Courtside Navy (#1B2A4A) full-bleed background to command authority at entry.\n- The timeline section alternates on Antique Linen (#EAE3D2) to provide visual separation and a warm archival feel.\n- The coaching grid returns to Crown Ivory, keeping the mid-page light and approachable.\n- The membership/pricing section uses Courtside Navy as a full-bleed dark background, creating a strong visual break and lending gravitas to the commercial proposition.\n- The facilities grid returns to Antique Linen, closing the page on a warm, reassuring note.\n- Championship Gold (#B8962E) is used consistently for ornamental rule lines, crest marks, badge accents, and decorative dividers throughout.\n- Burgundy Crest (#7D1D3F) is reserved for primary CTAs, active highlights, and ornamental flourishes at section transitions.\n- Forest Court (#2D5016) appears as tag/badge color on coaching credentials and facility category indicators.\n- Slate Mist (#D6D9E0) for all card borders, dividers, and input outlines.\n- Ink Smoke (#4A4E5A) for all secondary body copy, captions, and metadata labels.\n\n**Typography Hierarchy:**\n- All section eyebrows use Montserrat in small caps, uppercase, wide letter-spacing (0.15em+), set in Championship Gold \u2014 consistent across every section as a formal label system.\n- Section headlines use Playfair Display, set large and with tight tracking, in either Crown Ivory (on dark backgrounds) or Courtside Navy (on light backgrounds).\n- Subheadlines use Source Serif 4 in a medium italic weight at a comfortable reading size.\n- Body copy uses Source Serif 4 at 17\u201318px with line-height ~1.75, set in Ink Smoke on light backgrounds or Antique Linen/Slate Mist on dark.\n- Card titles use Playfair Display at H4 scale; card metadata/labels use Montserrat small caps.\n- CTA buttons use Montserrat uppercase with wide spacing, solid fills.\n\n**Card Grid System:**\nCards throughout the page share a consistent visual language: rounded corners (4\u20136px radius, restrained to avoid modern softness), a subtle 1px Slate Mist border, and on-hover a lift to Antique Linen background with a Championship Gold left-border accent. Cards on dark backgrounds invert to navy-on-ivory with gold accents. Cards maintain generous internal padding (24\u201332px) and clear typographic hierarchy within.\n\n**Symmetry & Ornamental Details:**\nEvery section header is horizontally centered with an ornamental Championship Gold rule line (thin, ~1px, 60px wide) placed between the eyebrow and the headline \u2014 a consistent decorative motif across all sections. Crest-like decorative marks (small symmetrical flourishes or laurel-adjacent SVG ornaments) appear at section transitions and at the top of the page header. The overall page composition is symmetrical: centered section headers, balanced card grids (2- or 4-column), and centered CTAs.\n\n**Layout Density & Spacing:**\nThis is a \"hard\" difficulty page with rich content. Sections use generous vertical padding (80\u2013100px top/bottom on desktop) to avoid crowding. Card grids breathe with 24\u201332px gutters. The timeline uses a center-spine layout on desktop. Responsive behavior: on tablet (\u22641024px), card grids collapse from 4-col to 2-col; on mobile (\u2264640px), all grids go to single column, the timeline spine collapses to a left-aligned list, and section padding reduces to 48\u201356px. Navigation and footer are inherited from the shared design system (Courtside Navy bar with Montserrat nav items and Championship Gold active underlines).\n\n**Page Fit Within Site:**\nAs the second page after Home, The Club page must validate the brand promise established on the landing page. It goes deeper and wider \u2014 more text, more structured information \u2014 but never loses the premium, heritage character. It should feel like the inside of a distinguished club: ordered, warm, and quietly impressive.",
