g dark/light/light/light/dark cadence gives the page a composed, editorial structure that mirrors a printed match programme.\n\nResponsive behavior: on desktop (\u22651200px), fixture and result cards display in a 2-column grid with generous gutters (32px). On tablet (768\u20131199px), cards collapse to a single column with tighter padding. On mobile (<768px), all cards are full-width stacked, stat figures remain prominent, and the filter/tag row wraps naturally. Navigation and footer are inherited from the shared design system (Courtside Navy bar, serif brand mark, gold rule accents).\n\nThis page fits the cross-site rhythm as the third page \u2014 following the Home landing and The Club overview \u2014 by shifting from aspirational and narrative tone to functional and informational. It should feel like opening a leather-bound club fixture booklet: structured, trustworthy, and rich with competitive heritage.",
